<title>USA: AEP 1,090 MW Cook 2 nuclear unit fully back.</title>
<headline>AEP 1,090 MW Cook 2 nuclear unit fully back.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Electric Power Co's (AEP) 1,090 megawatt (MW) unit 2 at its Donald Cook nuclear power plant resumed full output over the weekend, Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>Output of the Bridgman, Mich., unit was halved last week to repair both electronic feedwater pump controllers.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, at 1,020 MW, was operating at 93 percent of capacity.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
</text>
